  "body": "Not an Angular bug. The slider's native `change` event bubbles to the `mat-radio-group` `(change)`, which sets `useMajorityRatio` to `undefined` (no `.value` on that event). Guard it:\n\n```html\n(change)=\"$event.source && form.useMajorityRatio().value.set($event.value)\"\n```\n",
  "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
  "pin": null,
  "reactions": {
